  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "z[n] = x[n] + i*H{x}[n], the analytic signal",
        "The amplitude follows the envelope of the signal",
        "The change of the phase from sample to sample is the frequency"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How the library gets there",
      "items": [
        "Z[k] = 2*X[k] for a positive frequency, X[k] at bin 0 and the middle, 0 below",
        "Transform, weigh the bins, transform back; nothing is worked out in time",
        "The size must be a power of two, because the fft module asks for one"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What will catch you",
      "items": [
        "Both values mean something only where the signal holds one frequency at a time",
        "A signal of several frequencies gives a mean of them, which describes nothing",
        "That is why this goes together with emd, and hht joins the two"
      ]
    }
  ]
